		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Wailing ghost-woman born from drowning death.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 13, <strong>HP</strong> 29, <strong>ATK</strong> 3 touch +4 (1d8) or wail, <strong>MV</strong> double near (fly), <strong>S</strong> -4, <strong>D</strong> +3, <strong>C</strong> +2, <strong>I</strong> +0, <strong>W</strong> +0, <strong>Ch</strong> +4, <strong>AL</strong> <strong>C</strong>, <strong>LV</strong> 6</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Greater Undead</strong>. Immune to morale checks. Only damaged by silver or magical sources.</p><p></p><p><strong>Incorporeal</strong>. In place of attacks, become corporeal or incorporeal.</p><p></p><p><strong>Rejuvenation</strong>. If destroyed, reforms at her death site in 1d6 days. Bless or holy water stops reforming.</p><p></p><p><strong>Wail</strong>. All mortals within double near who can hear, WIS 15+, or attempt to drown themselves in the nearest body of water for 1d6 rounds.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
